From: Andrew Clunis <andrew@orospakr.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics - set the RMI4 doze interval Lenovo's driver uses on affected pads

On a Synaptics TM3471 (LEN2073, ThinkPad T14 Gen 2a AMD) driven over
RMI4/SMBus (InterTouch), the firmware's default doze settings lose most
short touches and corrupt the first frame of a two-finger touch:

  - 20 quick taps: 6 reach the kernel, each as a single ~15 ms frame;
    quarter-second taps fare no better.  Host Notify count, F12 frame
    count and evdev frame count agree, so the pad never reports them.
  - two-finger scrolls: about 1 in 10 lands with the two objects'
    positions swapped between the first and second frame, which
    libinput reads as a 2.5x change in finger separation and turns into
    a pinch.

Users see unreliable tap-to-click and scrolls that become pinches (or
right clicks).  The stock F01 doze registers on this pad are: interval 3,
wakeup threshold 45, holdoff 0, i.e. the sensor dozes the moment a finger
lifts.  Setting NoSleep fixes both symptoms but forbids doze entirely.

Lenovo's Windows driver package (SynPD.inf, AdjustFWDozeInterval_AddReg)
instead programs RMIDozeInterval = 6 for a list of twelve pad IDs,
LEN2073 among them, and leaves doze enabled.  Doing the same here gives
20 of 20 taps reported (60-190 ms, 4-10 frames each) and 0 pinches in
145 scroll episodes, against 6 of 20 and 1 in 10 before, with the doze
power saving intact.

Add the Windows list and pass doze_interval = 6 through the RMI4
platform data for those pads; rmi_f01 writes it at probe and re-applies
it on every configuration pass.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Clunis <andrew@orospakr.ca>
---
--- a/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/mouse/synaptics.c
@@ -204,6 +204,20 @@
 	"TOS0213", /* Dynabook Portege X30-D */
 	NULL
 };
+
+/*
+ * Pads whose firmware, left at its default doze settings, misses short
+ * touches and mangles the first frame of a two-finger touch when driven
+ * over RMI4/SMBus.  Lenovo's Windows driver (SynPD.inf,
+ * AdjustFWDozeInterval) programs an F01 doze interval of 6 on exactly
+ * these models; do the same.
+ */
+static const char * const rmi_doze_interval_pnp_ids[] = {
+	"LEN040D", "LEN040E", "LEN040F", "LEN0410", "LEN0411",
+	"LEN0417", "LEN0418",
+	"LEN2064", "LEN2073", "LEN2149", "LEN2161", "LEN2162",
+	NULL
+};
 #endif
 
 static const char * const forcepad_pnp_ids[] = {
@@ -1791,6 +1805,12 @@
 		!SYN_CAP_EXT_BUTTONS_STICK(info->ext_cap_10);
 	const struct rmi_device_platform_data pdata = {
 		.reset_delay_ms = 30,
+		.power_management = {
+			.doze_interval =
+				psmouse_matches_pnp_id(psmouse,
+						       rmi_doze_interval_pnp_ids) ?
+					6 : 0,
+		},
 		.sensor_pdata = {
 			.sensor_type = rmi_sensor_touchpad,
 			.axis_align.flip_y = true,
-- 
